From 8c007dcdafde326e38806479c28cae06cc17db02 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 02:43:25 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] :racehorse: Answer dma-buf requests from windows of guest
 RAM's files

RADV passes every imported buffer object with each submission, about
0.55 us each, and a busy macOS guest holds a thousand imports, 1.7 ms a
submission. With REIMS_VGPU_DMA_BUF_WINDOWS=1, a stretch of a request that
one run of a file covers, from a granule boundary, is an offset into a
dma-buf of the aligned window of that file it lies in (udmabuf's size
limit, 64 MiB by default), so every buffer over one window shares one
import: an 8 GiB guest is at most 128 imports. udmabuf pins a window's
pages whole, so the setting is off by default. It needs metal2vulkan's
chunks at offsets (DmaBufChunk::offset, DmaBufRequest::offset_alignment).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01GxoqC8ZLTGrUjAekESTLXh
